  <section id="about" class="reveal band">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 620px;">
      <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
      <p>I didn't start in AI. I spent years in ICT business development and enterprise sales — understanding client problems, negotiating solutions, and owning outcomes, not just code. That background shapes how I approach engineering today: every system starts with the business problem, not the tech stack.</p>
      <p>The shift began in data analysis — turning raw data into decisions for technical and non-technical stakeholders alike. From there, generative AI: building LLM-powered systems with RAG pipelines, vector search, and custom tool integrations. That naturally evolved into agentic engineering — designing multi-agent systems that reason, remember, and act, not just respond.</p>
      <p>Today I work as an Agentic AI Engineer at Bigello Digital, building production systems for real clients — and building toward the next stage: architecting agentic platforms at scale.</p>
